  "summary": "The great river of northern India and Bangladesh, rising in the Himalayas and reaching the Bay of Bengal through the world's largest delta. Hindus hold it sacred as the goddess Ganga, and hundreds of millions of people live on its plain. Rivers draining the rising Himalayas have carried sediment to the Bay of Bengal for roughly 20 million years; the present course is younger.",
